+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# [MP8] Exploding Collar Race 8-player adaptation — spawn points are placed by the user (user decision 2026-08-16)
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+#
+# **For this minigame the 8-player adaptation is almost entirely about spawn points**. Everything else scales naturally (diagnostic finding, probe44).
+#   · Mines are **procedurally generated** by `PoissonDiscSampling` over a polygon using `mine_distance`
+#     → the count follows the area, not the player count, so nothing needs changing.
+#   · The whole file has **no** fixed-length arrays indexed by player (only the spawn point array, grepped per pitfall #13).
+#   · There's only one harvester, and the end condition is `active_players.is_empty()` → independent of player count.
+#
+# ⚠️ Venue boundaries measured in practice (don't place anything outside them).
+#   The mine spawn transform is `Vector3(-8.0 + p.x, 0, -10.0 - p.y)`, p∈[0,16]×[0,80]
+#   → **the minefield covers x∈[-8,+8], z∈[-90,-10]**. Spawn points are at z≈+2~+7, i.e. **before** the minefield starts.
+#   · z too small (< -10) = spawning right inside the minefield.
+#   · z too large (≥ +10) = hitting `CameraTarget/KillArea` (the fall-behind-and-die zone), **dead the moment you spawn**.
+#   So positions are clamped to MP8_SPAWN_BOX, see below.
+#
+# The camera is at (0, 14, 8), yaw 0, pitch -58°, **looking toward -Z** → **screen left/right = world x**,
+# screen up/down = world z (up = toward the finish). During manual editing, directions are computed live from the camera basis vectors, not hardcoded.
+#
+# The 4 vanilla spawn points (true values measured by probe44).
+#   0 (-4.910, 1.947)   1 ( 1.443, 1.742)   2 (-4.793, 7.494)   3 ( 3.542, 7.364)
+# Default 8-player layout = **the 4 vanilla points untouched down to the byte** + 4 inserted within the span of their respective rows.
+const MP8_MAX_PLAYERS: int = 8
+const MP8_SPAWN_FILE: String = "user://mp8_mine_spawns.txt"
