+# ---- Widening the venue sideways (user 2026-08-16 - "widen the minefield and the vehicle together by 1.2x") ----
+#
+# ⚠️ **Widening only the minefield doesn't work**. This corridor is a tight fit (measured by probe45).
+#   Left wall inner face x=-8.06 / right wall inner face x=+7.99 (`Colliders/Walls`, 1 m thick ×105 long)
+#   Minefield x∈[-8,+8] — **sits right against both walls**
+#   Harvester KillArea Box 17 wide, x∈[-8.5,+8.5] — slightly wider than the corridor, so there's no getting around it
+#   Starting gate opening (the `StaticBody3D` pieces) gap x∈[-9.04,+7.52]
+# Widening only the mine polygon = mines get scattered into the walls, players are still boxed into 16 m, and gaps open up beside the harvester.
+# So **the whole corridor is scaled together** - art, walls, gate opening, finish/midpoint trigger areas, harvester.
+#
+# These top-level nodes are **not scaled**, because they are either in world coordinates or would distort players.
+#   `Players` (players would get squashed), `Mines` (mines are scattered in world coordinates), `player spawn positions`,
+#   `CameraTarget` (camera rig), `light parent` (scaling lights would skew the spotlight cones).
+const MP8_WIDE_DEFAULT: float = 1.2
+
+# 🩸 **Only nodes "containing nothing but meshes or BoxShape3D" can be scaled directly**.
+#
+# Godot **doesn't support non-uniform scaling of SphereShape3D / CapsuleShape3D / CylinderShape3D** —
+# scale them and the collision is broken. The first version set scale.x=1.2 on the whole of `StaticBody3D` and `Harvester`,
