+# ---- Placement-based scoring (user decision 2026-08-16) ----
+#
+# **Vanilla mechanics** (verified against the code, not copied from docs) - start at 0, with four ways to score —
+#   pass the midpoint +1 (once per player) / reach the finish +1 / **first** to arrive another +1 / arrive at full health another +1
+#   Max 4 points per round, and the default playlist has 3 rounds → 0~12 points.
+#   ⚠️ Old docs saying "max 3" are wrong, they missed the midpoint point.
+#
+# **The problem with 8 players** - 2nd place and 8th place score exactly the same, only 1st place gets 1 extra point —
+# 7 players can't be told apart, which is exactly the common flaw of the B (cumulative) family. And 3 rounds only yields 0~12,
+# worth even less than the A (placement) family (0~16), which only plays 2 rounds.
+#
+# **The fix** (the project's established approach - use indices into the minigame's own existing order arrays as scores,
+# instead of ranking integer counts at the tally stage). Exploding Collar Race **already has two real arrays appended in order**.
+#   `finished_players` — order of reaching the finish (vanilla already appends in order)
+#   `_mp8_dead_order`  — order of getting blown up (newly recorded by this mod, the only added mechanism)
+#
+# Ranking (D = number of deaths, F = number of finishers, D+F = players this round N)
+#   i-th to **die**     → i points        (0 … D-1, earliest deaths at the bottom)
+#   j-th to **finish**  → D + (F-1-j)     (D … N-1, first place gets N-1)
+#   → full range 0~N-1, **no repeats, no gaps, no ties**, measured with the same ruler as the A (placement) family.
+#   Plus **+1 for arriving at full health** (a skill bonus vanilla already has, only finishers can earn it) → max N.
+#
+# ⚠️ The midpoint +1 is **removed**. The dead are already ranked by death order, so its role is covered,
+#    and keeping it would only mess up the clean 0~N-1 range.
+# ⚠️ This **applies to every player count** (4-player match scoring changes too), same as was done for Junk Platform —
+#    no separate rule sets by player count, otherwise 4 and 8 players become two different games.
+var _mp8_dead_order: Array[int] = []
